LIB_LOAD("ihs",{"ihs1":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was the name of the town?","o":["Raymond","Vanity","Lagos","Zion"],"why":"An American town in the 1890s."},{"q":"Which Bible verse was Maxwell's sermon about?","o":["1 Peter 2:21, following in His steps","John 3:16","Psalm 23","Genesis 1:1"],"why":"\"...leaving us an example, that ye should follow his steps.\""},{"q":"What did the stranger ask Maxwell for on Friday?","o":["Help finding work","Money","Food","A coat"],"why":"He wanted a job."},{"q":"Why had the stranger lost his job?","o":["New printing machines replaced him","He was lazy","He was rude","He moved town"],"why":"It wasn't his fault."},{"q":"What song line did the stranger ask about?","o":["\"I'll go with Him, with Him, all the way\"","\"Amazing grace\"","\"Happy birthday\"","\"Jesus loves me\""],"why":"He asked if they really meant it."},{"q":"What did the stranger say would disappear if people lived out their songs?","o":["An awful lot of trouble in the world","All the churches","Music","Money"],"why":"Faith without action changes nothing."},{"q":"Where did the stranger spend his last week?","o":["In Maxwell's house","In hospital","On the street","In prison"],"why":"This time Maxwell opened his door."},{"q":"How long did the pledge last?","o":["One year","One week","One month","Ten years"],"why":"A year of asking \"What would Jesus do?\""},{"q":"Who was Rachel Winslow?","o":["A singer in the church","The editor","A rich man","The stranger's wife"],"why":"Her beautiful voice will face a big test."},{"q":"Complete: \"Faith, if it hath not ___, is dead.\"","o":["works","money","songs","friends"],"why":"James 2:17. Live it out!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What four letters do many people wear on bracelets, because of this book?","o":["WWJD","LOL","ABCD","OMG"],"why":"What Would Jesus Do? This book made the question famous."},"choices":[{"title":"The stranger after service","q":"After Sunday service, a young man in dirty clothes sits alone at the back of church. He looks hungry. Everyone walks past him.","o":[{"t":"Tell an usher or your parents, and help them get him some food and a kind word.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You noticed the knock at the door, and you got the right adults involved safely."},{"t":"Walk past like everyone else.","f":"That's closing the door, like Maxwell did on Friday."},{"t":"Whisper about him to your friends.","f":"He might be the most important person in the building today."}]},{"title":"Live the song","q":"You sing \"I surrender all\" in the youth choir on Sunday. On Monday, you're rude to a junior who bumps into you.","o":[{"t":"Apologise to the junior, and try to live what you sing.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Songs are meant to be lived out, not just sung."},{"t":"It's fine. It was only a junior.","f":"\"Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these...\""},{"t":"Stop singing in the choir.","f":"Don't stop singing. Start living it!"}]},{"title":"Hard questions","q":"In youth fellowship, a new member asks: \"Why do Christians in our school cheat in exams like everyone else?\" Some people get angry.","o":[{"t":"Listen humbly, admit it's a fair question, and talk about living it out.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The stranger's hard question changed a whole church. Don't silence it."},{"t":"Tell him to stop insulting Christians.","f":"First Church didn't throw the stranger out. His question was a gift."},{"t":"Change the subject.","f":"Hard questions help us grow. Face them."}]},{"title":"Take the pledge","q":"Your youth leader challenges everyone to ask \"What would Jesus do?\" before every choice for one week, including how you spend your data and pocket money.","o":[{"t":"Take it, write it down, and ask a friend to check on you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Ask the question, then do it, whatever it costs."},{"t":"Say yes, but don't really do it.","f":"The pledge had two parts: asking AND doing."},{"t":"Say no. It's too hard.","f":"Fifty people in Raymond said yes. You can too!"}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"church","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use In His Steps, Chapter 1 in real life."},{"sc":"door","n":"🚪 Notice the knock. The person in front of you might be your most important task today."},{"sc":"church","n":"🎶 Live the song. Don't just sing it or say it. Do it."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"🫶 Turn regret into action. Let mistakes change your direction."},{"sc":"church","n":"👣 Ask, then do. What would Jesus do? Then do it, whatever it costs."}],"stops":{"ihs1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"town","n":"This story happens long ago, in the 1890s, in an American town called {Raymond}."},{"sc":"study","n":"It's Friday morning. Rev. Henry Maxwell, pastor of the big, rich {First Church}, is in his study writing Sunday's sermon."},{"sc":"study","n":"His Bible is open at {1 Peter 2:21}: \"Christ also suffered for us, leaving us an example, that ye should follow his steps.\""},{"sc":"study","w":"maxwell","e":"smile","t":"Following in His steps. Yes, a beautiful sermon. The people will love it."},{"sc":"study","n":"Then the doorbell rings. Maxwell sighs. He's busy. He goes to the door."},{"sc":"door","n":"A young man stands outside. His clothes are old and dusty. He holds his worn-out hat in both hands."},{"sc":"door","w":"stranger","e":"worried","t":"Sir, I'm out of a job. I wondered if you might know of any work I could do. Anything at all."},{"sc":"door","w":"maxwell","e":"smile","t":"I'm sorry. I don't know of any work. Times are hard for many people. I hope you find something. Good morning."},{"sc":"door","n":"Maxwell closes the door. Through the window, he watches the young man walk slowly down the street."},{"sc":"study","n":"For a moment, Maxwell feels a little uncomfortable. Then he goes back to his desk, and to his sermon about following Jesus."}],"quote":{"text":"Christ also suffered for us, leaving us an example, that ye should follow his steps.","who":"1 Peter 2:21","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Notice the knock","text":"Maxwell was writing about following Jesus at the very moment Jesus' kind of chance was knocking at his door, and he was too busy to see it. Leaders don't only talk about doing good. They notice the person standing in front of them."},"think":"Has anyone ever needed your help when you were 'too busy'? What would you do differently now?","quiz":[{"q":"Where does this story happen?","o":["In an American town called Raymond, in the 1890s","In Lagos today","In the City of Destruction","In London"],"why":"It's a true-to-life story set in America long ago."},{"q":"What was Maxwell writing when the stranger knocked?","o":["A sermon about following in Jesus' steps","A shopping list","A letter to his mother","A newspaper story"],"why":"He was writing about following Jesus."},{"q":"What did the young man ask for?","o":["Help finding work","Money for food","A place to sleep","A Bible"],"why":"He wanted a job, anything at all."},{"q":"What did Maxwell do?","o":["Said sorry, he didn't know of any work, and closed the door","Gave him a job","Invited him in","Called the police"],"why":"He was polite, but too busy to really help."},{"q":"How did Maxwell feel afterwards?","o":["A little uncomfortable, but he went back to work","Very happy","Angry","Nothing at all"],"why":"His conscience nudged him, but he ignored it, for now."}]},"ihs1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"Sunday morning. First Church is full of well-dressed people. The windows are beautiful. The choir is the best in town."},{"sc":"church","n":"A young woman named {Rachel Winslow} sings a solo. Her voice is amazing. The song says: \"Where He leads me I will follow, I'll go with Him, with Him, all the way.\""},{"sc":"church","n":"Then Maxwell preaches his sermon on following Jesus' steps. Everyone agrees it's excellent."},{"sc":"church","n":"Just as the service is ending, something happens that has never happened in First Church before. A young man stands up at the back and walks down the middle aisle."},{"sc":"church","n":"It's the stranger from Friday. His clothes are still dusty. People stare. Nobody moves to stop him."},{"sc":"church","w":"stranger","e":"worried","t":"I'm not drunk, and I'm not crazy. I just want to say something, since I may never get another chance."},{"sc":"church","w":"stranger","e":"worried","t":"I was a {printer}. When new {printing machines} came, I lost my job, like many others. I've been looking for work for ten months."},{"sc":"church","w":"stranger","e":"worried","t":"My wife died a few months ago, in a crowded little room in the city. My little girl is staying with friends until I can find work."},{"sc":"church","w":"stranger","e":"worried","t":"I'm not complaining. But I keep wondering: what do you Christians mean when you sing, \"I'll go with Him, with Him, all the way\"?"},{"sc":"church","w":"stranger","e":"worried","t":"It seems to me there's an awful lot of trouble in the world that somehow wouldn't exist if all the people who sing such songs went and lived them out.","b":true},{"sc":"church","n":"Then he sways... and falls to the floor, right in front of the pulpit."}],"quote":{"text":"It seems to me there's an awful lot of trouble in the world that somehow wouldn't exist if all the people who sing such songs went and lived them out.","who":"Stranger","tag":"Sheldon's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Live the song","text":"The choir sang about following Jesus all the way. The pastor preached about it. But a hungry man had knocked on their doors all week, and nobody really helped. Leaders don't just sing it or say it. They live it, especially when it costs them something."},"think":"Which song or Bible verse do you love? What would it look like to actually live it out this week?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Rachel Winslow sing?","o":["\"Where He leads me I will follow, I'll go with Him all the way\"","A love song","A war song","Nothing"],"why":"A beautiful song about following Jesus."},{"q":"What did the stranger do at the end of the service?","o":["Walked down the aisle and spoke to the church","Stole the offering","Fell asleep","Sang a song"],"why":"Nothing like that had ever happened in First Church."},{"q":"Why did he lose his job as a printer?","o":["New printing machines replaced many printers","He was lazy","He stole","He was sick"],"why":"Machines took his job, through no fault of his own."},{"q":"What question did he ask?","o":["What do Christians mean when they sing \"I'll go with Him all the way\"?","Can I have money?","Where is the toilet?","Who is the pastor?"],"why":"He wanted to know if they meant what they sang."},{"q":"What happened after he finished speaking?","o":["He fell to the floor","He walked out","Everyone clapped","He sang"],"why":"He was weak, hungry and sick."}]},"ihs1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"People rush forward. A doctor in the congregation checks the young man. He's very weak and ill."},{"sc":"church","w":"maxwell","e":"worried","t":"Take him to my house. We'll look after him there."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"For the whole week, the young man lies in Maxwell's guest room. The best doctor in town treats him. Maxwell's wife sits with him."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"Maxwell visits him every day. Every time he looks at the young man's face, he remembers closing the door on him on Friday."},{"sc":"sickroom","w":"maxwell","e":"worried","t":"I wrote a whole sermon about following Jesus... and I shut the door on the very person Jesus would have helped."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"The young man thanks them for their kindness. He talks a little about his little girl, and asks them to make sure she's cared for."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"On the next Sunday morning, very early, the young man dies peacefully. Maxwell is beside him."},{"sc":"study","n":"Maxwell sits alone in his study for a long time. He can't stop thinking about the young man's question."},{"sc":"study","w":"maxwell","e":"worried","t":"What DO we mean when we sing those songs? What would it look like if we really followed in His steps?"},{"sc":"study","n":"He prays for a long time. And slowly, an idea grows in his heart, an idea that scares him a little."}],"quote":{"text":"Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.","who":"Jesus (Matthew 25:40)","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Let regret turn into action","text":"Maxwell couldn't undo closing the door. But he didn't just feel bad and move on. He took the young man home, cared for him, and let the pain change him. Leaders let their mistakes teach them, and they turn regret into a new direction."},"think":"Is there a mistake that taught you something important? How did it change what you do now?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was the young man taken after he fell?","o":["To Maxwell's house","To a prison","To the train station","Back to the street"],"why":"This time, Maxwell opened his door."},{"q":"What did Maxwell keep remembering?","o":["Closing the door on him on Friday","His sermon notes","His holiday","The choir"],"why":"His conscience was speaking loudly now."},{"q":"What did the young man ask them to do?","o":["Make sure his little girl was cared for","Find him a job","Give him money","Call his boss"],"why":"Even at the end, he thought of his daughter."},{"q":"What happened the next Sunday morning?","o":["The young man died peacefully","He got a job","He left town","He became a pastor"],"why":"A sad ending that changed everything."},{"q":"What did Maxwell do afterwards?","o":["Prayed for a long time, and an idea grew in his heart","Forgot about it","Went on holiday","Left the church"],"why":"Regret turned into a new direction."}]},"ihs1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"The next Sunday, First Church is full again. Everyone has heard about the stranger. The room is very quiet."},{"sc":"church","w":"maxwell","e":"stern","t":"What happened here last week has made me ask myself what it really means to follow Jesus. So I have something to ask of you."},{"sc":"church","w":"maxwell","e":"stern","t":"I want volunteers who will promise, honestly, for an entire year, not to do anything without first asking the question: 'What would Jesus do?'","b":true},{"sc":"church","w":"maxwell","e":"stern","t":"And after asking that question, each one will follow Jesus as exactly as he knows how, no matter what the result may be."},{"sc":"church","n":"Nobody moves. It's a big {pledge}. Following Jesus that closely might cost them their money, their friends, or their jobs."},{"sc":"church","n":"After the service, Maxwell asks anyone who wants to take the pledge to stay behind. He's not sure anyone will."},{"sc":"church","n":"Then they come, one by one. Rachel Winslow, the singer. Edward Norman, the editor of the town newspaper. Alexander Powers, who runs the railway workshops."},{"sc":"church","n":"Donald Marsh, the president of the college. Milton Wright, a businessman. Jasper Chase, a writer. Virginia Page, a very rich young woman. And many more: about fifty people in all!"},{"sc":"church","w":"norman","e":"stern","t":"I don't know where this will lead. But I'm going to do it."},{"sc":"church","w":"rachel","e":"smile","t":"Me too. Whatever it costs."},{"sc":"church","n":"They kneel and pray together. Something powerful fills the room. They feel the Holy Spirit with them, as never before."},{"sc":"church","n":"None of them knows yet how much their lives are about to change. Find out what happens to the editor and the railway man in Chapter 2!"}],"quote":{"text":"Not to do anything without first asking the question, 'What would Jesus do?'","who":"Maxwell","tag":"Sheldon's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Ask the question, then do it","text":"The pledge had two parts. First, ask honestly: what would Jesus do here? Second, do it, whatever it costs. Most people stop at the first part. Leaders who follow in His steps do both, and they invite others to join them."},"think":"Pick one situation this week, at school, at home or online. What would Jesus do? Will you do it?","quiz":[{"q":"What question did Maxwell ask volunteers to ask before everything?","o":["\"What would Jesus do?\"","\"What will people think?\"","\"How much will it cost?\"","\"Is it fun?\""],"why":"The question at the heart of the whole book."},{"q":"How long was the pledge for?","o":["One whole year","One day","One week","Forever"],"why":"A full year of asking, and doing."},{"q":"What was the second part of the pledge?","o":["Follow Jesus as exactly as you know how, no matter the result","Tell everyone about it","Give all your money away","Stop working"],"why":"Asking isn't enough. You have to do it."},{"q":"Who was Edward Norman?","o":["The editor of the town newspaper","The singer","The stranger","The pastor"],"why":"His job is about to get very interesting."},{"q":"About how many people took the pledge?","o":["About fifty","Two","Five hundred","Nobody"],"why":"About fifty brave people stayed behind."}]}}},"ihs2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Norman refuse to print first?","o":["A report on a brutal prize fight","The church news","The weather","A love story"],"why":"The first test of his pledge."},{"q":"Who was Mr Clark?","o":["The managing editor at the newspaper","A railway worker","The pastor","A singer"],"why":"He couldn't believe what Norman was doing!"},{"q":"Why did Norman stop the Sunday edition?","o":["So his workers could rest and worship on Sunday","To save paper","Nobody bought it","The printer broke"],"why":"He cared about his workers."},{"q":"What happened to the Daily News after Norman's changes?","o":["Many people cancelled, but new readers came because they trusted it","It became the richest paper","Nothing changed","It closed at once"],"why":"Integrity cost money, but built trust."},{"q":"\"Ye cannot serve God and ___.\"","o":["mammon","man","music","markets"],"why":"Matthew 6:24. Mammon means money and riches."},{"q":"What did Powers create for his workers?","o":["A lunch room with coffee","A football field","A school","A bank"],"why":"Small service, big impact."},{"q":"How did Powers find the secret papers?","o":["They were sent to him by mistake","He spied on his boss","A friend gave them to him","He found them in a bin"],"why":"The truth came to him unexpectedly."},{"q":"Where did Powers send the papers?","o":["To the government office in charge of railways","To his wife","To the newspaper","Back to the company"],"why":"The right channel."},{"q":"How did Powers' family feel at first?","o":["Upset about what they'd lose","Happy","They didn't care","Proud"],"why":"Doing right can be hard for the people around you too."},{"q":"\"The ___ of the upright shall guide them.\"","o":["integrity","money","friends","strength"],"why":"Proverbs 11:3."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What famous four-word question did both men keep asking?","o":["What would Jesus do?","How much will it cost?","Who will find out?","What will people say?"],"why":"Ask it, then do it!"},"choices":[{"title":"Your front page","q":"You run a popular class WhatsApp news page. Someone sends you a video of two students fighting. If you post it, it'll get hundreds of views.","o":[{"t":"Don't post it. Delete it, and tell a teacher if someone is in danger.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Norman with the prize fight: not everything that sells should be shared."},{"t":"Post it. People want to see it.","f":"That's printing the prize fight. Every share is your front page."},{"t":"Post it with a funny caption.","f":"Mocking people's pain is never news Jesus would share."}]},{"title":"The sponsor","q":"Your school football club is offered free jerseys by a betting company, if the company's logo goes on the front.","o":[{"t":"Kindly decline, and look for other sponsors, like local businesses or old students.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Norman with the adverts: no money for things that hurt people."},{"t":"Accept. Free jerseys are free jerseys.","f":"You can't serve two masters. Advertising betting to teenagers hurts people."},{"t":"Accept, but hide the logo with tape.","f":"That's taking the money and pretending you didn't."}]},{"title":"The empty room","q":"You're the class prefect. Juniors have nowhere to eat lunch when it rains, so they eat standing in the corridor.","o":[{"t":"Ask a teacher if an empty classroom can be opened for them at lunch.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! That's Powers' coffee room. Use your position to serve."},{"t":"It's not your problem. You're not a junior.","f":"Leaders notice the needs of the people under them."},{"t":"Tell them to stop complaining.","f":"Powers didn't wait for complaints. He noticed and acted."}]},{"title":"The envelope","q":"You discover that the class treasurer has been secretly taking money from the class dues. You have screenshots that prove it.","o":[{"t":"Calmly show the proof to your class teacher, without posting it publicly.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Powers: report wrongdoing through the right channel, not the rumour mill."},{"t":"Post the screenshots in the class group.","f":"Powers didn't print it in the newspaper. He went to the proper office."},{"t":"Say nothing. It's not your money.","f":"Integrity means doing right, even when it's uncomfortable."},{"t":"Ask the treasurer to share the money with you.","f":"That turns you into part of the problem."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"newsroom","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use In His Steps, Chapter 2 in real life."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"📰 You're a publisher. Before you post or share, ask: would Jesus be glad to see this on my front page?"},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"⚖️ One master. Decide now that money and popularity don't get the final say."},{"sc":"workshop","n":"☕ Serve from your position. Notice small needs, and meet them."},{"sc":"office","n":"✉️ Do right when nobody's watching, and report wrongdoing the right way."}],"stops":{"ihs2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"newsroom","n":"Monday morning. Edward Norman, the {editor} and owner of the {Raymond Daily News}, walks into his office. He took the pledge yesterday."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"The newsroom is noisy: typewriters clicking, boys running with papers, the big printing press rumbling downstairs."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"Mr Clark, the managing editor, hurries in with a long report. It's about a famous {prize fight} that happened on Saturday."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"clark","e":"big","t":"This is the big story, sir! Every paper in the country will run it. Readers love this stuff. It'll sell thousands of copies!"},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"Norman reads it. It's a description of two men beating each other bloody, for money, while crowds cheer."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"stern","t":"What would Jesus do?"},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"He thinks for a long time. Then he hands the report back."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"stern","t":"We won't print it, Clark. I don't believe Jesus would print this in His newspaper."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"clark","e":"shock","t":"Not print it?! Sir, our readers will be furious! They'll buy another paper!"},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"smile","t":"Maybe. But from today, this paper will only print what I believe Jesus would be glad to see in it."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"Clark walks out shaking his head. The next morning, the other papers are full of the fight. The Daily News isn't."}],"quote":{"text":"Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest... think on these things.","who":"Philippians 4:8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Choose what you put out there","text":"Norman's newspaper reached thousands of people. When he asked \"What would Jesus do?\", he realised that what he printed was shaping his whole town. Today, YOU are a publisher too: every post, share and forward is your 'front page'. Leaders choose content that builds people up."},"think":"If Jesus scrolled through everything you've posted or shared this month, what would He be glad to see? What would you take down?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Edward Norman's job?","o":["Editor and owner of the town newspaper","A pastor","A railway boss","A singer"],"why":"He ran the Raymond Daily News."},{"q":"What story did Mr Clark want to print?","o":["A report on a brutal prize fight","A church announcement","A weather report","A football match"],"why":"A violent story that would sell many papers."},{"q":"What did Norman ask himself?","o":["\"What would Jesus do?\"","\"How much will this make?\"","\"What will Clark think?\"","\"What do readers want?\""],"why":"The question from his pledge."},{"q":"What did Norman decide?","o":["Not to print it","To print it on the front page","To print it in small letters","To sell it to another paper"],"why":"He didn't believe Jesus would print it."},{"q":"How is YOUR phone like Norman's newspaper?","o":["What you post and share shapes the people who see it","It isn't at all","Phones print paper","Only adults have phones"],"why":"Every share is your 'front page'."}]},"ihs2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"newsroom","n":"That was only the beginning. Over the next weeks, Norman keeps asking the question, about everything in the paper."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"stern","t":"Our Sunday edition makes our workers work every Sunday, and stops them resting and going to church. Would Jesus run it? I don't think so. We'll stop it."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"clark","e":"shock","t":"But that's some of our best money, sir!"},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"Then Norman looks at the advertisements. Some are for alcohol and tobacco. Some are for things that cheat people."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"stern","t":"Would Jesus take money to advertise things that hurt people? No. Take those adverts out."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"He also decides that the paper will stop blindly supporting one political party. It will tell the truth about every side."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"The results come quickly. Hundreds of {subscribers} cancel. Some advertisers leave. People laugh at him in the street. \"Norman's gone soft!\""},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"clark","e":"worried","t":"Sir, we're losing money every week. If this goes on, the paper could close!"},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"smile","t":"Then it closes. But I'd rather lose the paper than run it in a way Jesus wouldn't. I'm not giving up."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"And slowly, something else happens. Some new readers start buying the Daily News, because they trust it. It's honest. It's different."}],"quote":{"text":"No man can serve two masters... Ye cannot serve God and mammon.","who":"Matthew 6:24","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Integrity costs, and it's worth it","text":"Asking \"What would Jesus do?\" cost Norman money, readers and respect. But it gave his town something rare: a newspaper people could trust. Leaders decide ahead of time that money doesn't get the final say. One master, not two."},"think":"Is there something you'd be tempted to do 'because it makes money' or 'because everyone does it'? What would Jesus do?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Norman stop the Sunday edition?","o":["It made his workers work every Sunday","Nobody read it","It was too expensive to print","Clark asked him to"],"why":"He cared about his workers' rest and worship."},{"q":"Which adverts did he take out?","o":["Adverts for things that hurt people, like alcohol and tobacco","All adverts","Adverts for food","Church adverts"],"why":"He wouldn't take money for harm."},{"q":"What happened to his subscribers?","o":["Hundreds cancelled","They doubled","Nothing changed","They all moved away"],"why":"Integrity has a cost."},{"q":"What did Norman say he would rather do than run the paper wrongly?","o":["Lose the paper","Sell the paper","Move to another town","Give up the pledge"],"why":"Money didn't get the final say."},{"q":"What does \"mammon\" mean in Matthew 6:24?","o":["Money and riches","A kind of food","A city","A king"],"why":"You can't serve God and money as masters at the same time."}]},"ihs2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"workshop","n":"Across town, Alexander Powers also took the pledge. He's the {superintendent} of the {railway workshops}: hundreds of men work under him, building and repairing trains."},{"sc":"workshop","n":"It's loud, hot, dirty work. At lunchtime, the men eat sitting on the floor, on boxes, or squeezed next to the machines."},{"sc":"workshop","w":"powers","e":"worried","t":"What would Jesus do, if He were in charge of these men?"},{"sc":"workshop","n":"Powers remembers a big empty room upstairs in the workshop building. Nobody uses it."},{"sc":"workshop","w":"powers","e":"smile","t":"Let's clean that room out, put in tables and chairs, and make it a place where the men can eat lunch in peace. I'll make sure there's hot coffee too."},{"sc":"workshop","n":"The men are surprised. Their boss has never done anything like this before! The room fills up at lunchtime."},{"sc":"workshop","w":"worker","e":"big","t":"A proper place to sit and eat? With coffee? The boss did this for us?"},{"sc":"workshop","n":"Powers invites Rev. Maxwell to come and give a short talk during lunch. Maxwell is nervous. He has never spoken to working men like these."},{"sc":"workshop","n":"But the men listen, and they're grateful. The room becomes a place where the bosses and workers start to see each other as people."}],"quote":{"text":"As we have therefore opportunity, let us do good unto all men.","who":"Galatians 6:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Use your position to serve","text":"Powers didn't make a speech or start a big programme. He looked at the people under him, saw what they needed, and used what he had: an empty room and some coffee. Leaders notice the small, everyday needs of the people they lead, and meet them."},"think":"If you're a prefect, captain, class rep or older sibling, what small thing could you do to make life better for the people 'under' you?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Alexander Powers' job?","o":["Superintendent of the railway workshops","Newspaper editor","Train driver","Pastor"],"why":"He was the boss of hundreds of workers."},{"q":"Where did the workers eat lunch before?","o":["On the floor, on boxes, or next to the machines","In a restaurant","At home","In the church"],"why":"Nobody had thought about their comfort."},{"q":"What did Powers do?","o":["Turned an empty room into a lunch room with coffee","Gave everyone a pay rise","Shut the workshop","Bought a new train"],"why":"He used what he had to serve them."},{"q":"Who did Powers invite to speak to the men?","o":["Rev. Maxwell","Edward Norman","Rachel Winslow","Mr Clark"],"why":"And the men listened."},{"q":"What is the main lesson?","o":["Use your position to serve the people under you","Bosses should never talk to workers","Coffee is important","Work is boring"],"why":"Small acts of service from leaders mean a lot."}]},"ihs2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"office","n":"A few weeks later, Powers is sorting his mail. One large envelope was sent to him by mistake. It was meant for somebody else in the company."},{"sc":"office","n":"He opens it, then realises what he's reading. The papers prove that the railway company has been secretly breaking the law, cheating the public and the government."},{"sc":"office","w":"powers","e":"shock","t":"This is clear proof. The company I work for is breaking the law, on purpose."},{"sc":"office","n":"Powers knows what this means. If he hands these papers to the authorities, he'll lose his job, his big salary, his fine house, and his place among the important people of Raymond."},{"sc":"office","w":"powers","e":"worried","t":"If I keep quiet, nobody will ever know. My family will be comfortable. But... what would Jesus do?"},{"sc":"office","n":"He goes home and tells his wife and daughter. They're upset. \"Think of us! Think of everything we'll lose!\""},{"sc":"office","n":"Powers prays for a long time. It is the hardest choice of his life."},{"sc":"office","w":"powers","e":"stern","t":"I can't pretend I didn't see it. Jesus wouldn't cover up a lie to keep a good job."},{"sc":"office","n":"So he sends the papers to the {Interstate Commerce Commission}, the government office in charge. Then he resigns from the railway."},{"sc":"office","n":"He loses his big job and his position in society. Some of his friends stop speaking to him. He goes back to his old work as a {telegraph operator}, earning much less."},{"sc":"office","w":"powers","e":"smile","t":"My pay is smaller. But my conscience is clear. And I can look Jesus in the face."}],"quote":{"text":"The integrity of the upright shall guide them.","who":"Proverbs 11:3","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Do right when nobody's watching","text":"Nobody would have known if Powers kept quiet. That's exactly what made it a real test. He reported the wrongdoing through the right channel, quietly and properly, and paid a heavy price. Leaders with integrity do the right thing even when it costs them, and even when nobody would ever find out."},"think":"Is there a time you did the right thing when nobody would have known? How did it feel?","quiz":[{"q":"How did the papers reach Powers?","o":["In an envelope sent to him by mistake","He stole them","Norman gave them to him","He found them on the street"],"why":"He wasn't looking for trouble. It found him."},{"q":"What did the papers prove?","o":["The railway company was secretly breaking the law","His workers were lazy","The trains were broken","Maxwell was wrong"],"why":"Clear proof of wrongdoing."},{"q":"What would Powers lose if he reported it?","o":["His job, salary, house and social position","Nothing","Only a little money","His church"],"why":"A very heavy price."},{"q":"What did Powers do with the papers?","o":["Sent them to the government office in charge, and resigned","Burned them","Hid them","Posted them in the newspaper"],"why":"He reported it the right way, through the proper channel."},{"q":"What job did Powers go back to?","o":["Telegraph operator","Pastor","Farmer","Editor"],"why":"Smaller pay, but a clear conscience."}]}}},"ihs3":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did the opera company offer Rachel?","o":["A big salary to sing on stage across America","A house","A newspaper","A train"],"why":"Money and fame."},{"q":"Why did Rachel say no?","o":["She believed her gift was mainly for helping people","She was scared","The pay was too low","She disliked music"],"why":"It was about the purpose of her gift."},{"q":"What was the Rectangle?","o":["The poorest, roughest part of Raymond","A big church","A school","A railway station"],"why":"The place most church people avoided."},{"q":"Who preached in the tent?","o":["Mr Gray","Mr Clark","Alexander Powers","Rollin Page"],"why":"An evangelist in the Rectangle."},{"q":"What happened when Rachel sang in the tent?","o":["Everyone went silent and listened","People walked out","A fight started","Nothing changed"],"why":"Her gift was where it was needed."},{"q":"Who took Loreen home?","o":["Virginia Page","Rachel","Mr Gray","Mrs Winslow"],"why":"She opened her own home."},{"q":"How did Virginia's grandmother feel about Loreen moving in?","o":["Horrified","Happy","Bored","Excited"],"why":"Doing right can shock people."},{"q":"What did Rachel tell Rollin his life lacked?","o":["A real purpose","Money","Friends","Clothes"],"why":"Honest words that changed him."},{"q":"Who did Rollin decide to reach with the gospel?","o":["The rich young men at his old clubs","The railway workers","Children only","Nobody"],"why":"His own people."},{"q":"Complete: \"If any man be in Christ, he is a new ___.\"","o":["creature","house","song","town"],"why":"2 Corinthians 5:17."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Which famous question did Rachel, Virginia and Rollin all ask?","o":["What would Jesus do?","What would Mother say?","How much does it pay?","Who's watching?"],"why":"The question that changed Raymond."},"choices":[{"title":"Your gift, your choice","q":"You sing really well. A popular producer offers to make you famous online, but only if you sing a song with dirty lyrics in a music video.","o":[{"t":"Say no, and keep using your voice for songs that build people up.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Rachel: your gift is from God, and you get to choose what it's for."},{"t":"Do it once to get famous, then change later.","f":"Rachel didn't trade her gift's purpose for fame, even once."},{"t":"Stop singing altogether.","f":"Don't bury the gift. Use it well!"}]},{"title":"Go to the Rectangle","q":"Your youth group is planning an outreach with food and songs at a nearby motor park. You're nervous because the area is rough.","o":[{"t":"Go with the group and the adult leaders, and use your gift there.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Rachel and Virginia went to the Rectangle, together and safely, with Mr Gray."},{"t":"Stay home. Let other people go.","f":"The people who need hope most are often in the places we avoid."},{"t":"Go alone at night to prove you're brave.","f":"Brave isn't the same as careless. Go with the team and the adults."}]},{"title":"A second chance","q":"A classmate with a bad reputation starts coming to your Scripture Union meetings. Some members whisper, \"What is SHE doing here?\"","o":[{"t":"Welcome her warmly, sit with her, and help her feel at home.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Nobody is a hopeless case. Be her Virginia."},{"t":"Join the whispering.","f":"That's Virginia's grandmother: \"What will people say?\""},{"t":"Ignore her and hope she leaves.","f":"Loreen needed a home and a friend, not silence."}]},{"title":"No purpose?","q":"It's the long holiday. You've spent three weeks sleeping late and scrolling. A friend asks, \"What are you actually doing with your life?\"","o":[{"t":"Set a goal: learn a skill, read a book, or volunteer somewhere.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Rollin, honest words can wake you up to a purpose."},{"t":"Get angry at your friend.","f":"Rollin could have been angry with Rachel. Instead, he listened."},{"t":"Keep scrolling. It's the holidays.","f":"Rest is good, but you were made for good works too."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"tent","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use In His Steps, Chapter 3 in real life."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"🎤 Your gift isn't just for you. Ask what God gave it to you FOR."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"⛺ Take it where it's needed. The best stage may be the place everyone avoids."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"🌸 Nobody is a hopeless case. Give people room to start again."},{"sc":"town","n":"🎯 Find your purpose. Start with the people you can reach better than anyone else."}],"stops":{"ihs3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"parlour","n":"Rachel Winslow has the most beautiful voice in Raymond. People say she could be famous anywhere in the country."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"One morning, a letter arrives from a famous {opera company}. They want Rachel to join them and sing on stage in cities all over America."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"mrswinslow","e":"big","t":"Rachel! Look at this salary! It's more money than most men earn. You'll be famous! This is the chance of a lifetime!"},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rachel","e":"worried","t":"It IS a wonderful offer, Mother. But I made a promise in church. I have to ask: what would Jesus do?"},{"sc":"parlour","n":"Rachel thinks and prays about it for days. Singing isn't wrong. Her voice is a gift from God. The question is: what does God want her to do with it?"},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rachel","e":"stern","t":"If Jesus had a voice like mine, I don't believe He would use it mainly to make money and fame for Himself. I believe He would use it to help people."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rachel","e":"smile","t":"I'm going to say no to the opera company. I want my voice to be used for God, wherever He sends me."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"mrswinslow","e":"frown","t":"Say no?! Rachel, you're throwing away your future! What will people say?"},{"sc":"parlour","n":"Rachel's mother is very disappointed. Some of her friends think she's foolish. But Rachel writes the letter, and turns the offer down."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"She doesn't yet know where God will lead her voice. But she's about to find out, in the last place anyone would expect."}],"quote":{"text":"As every man hath received the gift, even so minister the same one to another.","who":"1 Peter 4:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Your gift isn't just for you","text":"Rachel didn't say singing was bad, or that money was evil. She asked a deeper question: what was her gift FOR? She decided God gave her voice to help others, not mainly to make herself rich and famous. Leaders know their gifts come from God, and they ask how to use them for His purposes."},"think":"What's your gift: singing, drawing, football, maths, making people laugh? How could you use it to help others?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Rachel Winslow's gift?","o":["A beautiful singing voice","Writing newspapers","Running fast","Building trains"],"why":"The best voice in Raymond."},{"q":"What did the opera company offer her?","o":["A big salary to sing on stage all over America","A free house","A job as a teacher","A trip to Africa"],"why":"Money and fame, the chance of a lifetime."},{"q":"How did her mother react?","o":["Thrilled, and then disappointed when Rachel said no","Angry from the start","She didn't care","She cried with joy at the refusal"],"why":"She thought Rachel was throwing away her future."},{"q":"What question did Rachel ask?","o":["\"What would Jesus do?\"","\"How much will I earn?\"","\"What will my friends think?\"","\"Where is the stage?\""],"why":"The question from her pledge."},{"q":"Why did Rachel turn the offer down?","o":["She believed God gave her voice mainly to help people","She hated singing","The money was too small","She was scared of the stage"],"why":"It was about the purpose of her gift."}]},"ihs3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"rectangle","n":"On the edge of Raymond is a district called {the Rectangle}. It's the poorest, roughest part of town, full of {saloons}, gambling, fighting and hunger."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"Most church people in Raymond never go there. They pretend it isn't there."},{"sc":"tent","n":"But an {evangelist} named Mr Gray has put up a big tent right in the middle of the Rectangle. Every night he preaches there."},{"sc":"tent","w":"virginia","e":"smile","t":"Rachel, let's go to Mr Gray's tent tonight. He needs help. And you could sing."},{"sc":"tent","n":"So Rachel and Virginia go into the Rectangle at night. The tent is full of rough men and tired women. Some are drunk. Some are shouting and laughing."},{"sc":"tent","n":"Mr Gray tries to preach, but it's hard to be heard. Then Rachel stands up, and begins to sing."},{"sc":"tent","n":"The tent goes completely silent. Men stop laughing. A woman stops crying. Nobody in the Rectangle has ever heard anything like it."},{"sc":"tent","w":"gray","e":"smile","t":"Thank God for that voice. These people listened to you tonight like they've never listened before."},{"sc":"tent","n":"Night after night, Rachel comes back to sing. The crowds get bigger. When Mr Gray's voice gets tired and fails, Rachel's singing keeps the meetings going."},{"sc":"tent","w":"rachel","e":"big","t":"THIS is where my voice belongs. Not on a stage for money, but here, where people need hope."}],"quote":{"text":"He hath put a new song in my mouth, even praise unto our God: many shall see it, and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.","who":"Psalm 40:3","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Take your gift where it's needed","text":"The same voice that could have filled grand theatres filled a dusty tent in the worst part of town, and it changed people's lives. Rachel didn't wait for the Rectangle to come to church. She went to the Rectangle. Leaders take their gifts to the places most people avoid."},"think":"Where is the 'Rectangle' near you: a place or group of people everyone avoids? What could your gift do there?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the Rectangle?","o":["The poorest, roughest part of Raymond","A shape in maths class","A rich neighbourhood","A church"],"why":"Saloons, gambling, fighting and hunger."},{"q":"Who had put up a tent in the Rectangle?","o":["Mr Gray, an evangelist","Rachel","Edward Norman","Alexander Powers"],"why":"He preached there every night."},{"q":"Who invited Rachel to come and sing?","o":["Virginia Page","Her mother","Mr Clark","Rollin Page"],"why":"Virginia went with her."},{"q":"What happened when Rachel sang?","o":["The noisy tent went completely silent","People threw things","Everyone left","Nothing"],"why":"Nobody there had ever heard anything like it."},{"q":"Where did Rachel decide her voice belonged?","o":["Where people needed hope, like the tent","On a big stage for money","Only in church","Nowhere"],"why":"Gifts belong where they're needed."}]},"ihs3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"tent","n":"One night, a woman named {Loreen} stumbles into the tent. She is drunk. Her clothes are torn. Everyone in the Rectangle knows her as a hopeless case."},{"sc":"tent","n":"Rachel sings. Loreen sits very still. Then she starts to cry, and she can't stop."},{"sc":"tent","w":"loreen","e":"worried","t":"Is it true? Could God really want somebody like me?"},{"sc":"tent","w":"gray","e":"smile","t":"Yes, Loreen. Jesus came for exactly people like you, and like me."},{"sc":"tent","n":"That night, Loreen kneels and prays. She asks God to forgive her and give her a new life."},{"sc":"tent","n":"But after the meeting, she has nowhere safe to go. If she goes back to the saloons, she'll fall back into her old life."},{"sc":"tent","w":"virginia","e":"stern","t":"What would Jesus do? He would give her a home. Loreen, come and live with me."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"Virginia takes Loreen home to her beautiful mansion. Virginia's grandmother is horrified. \"A woman like THAT, in OUR house? What will people say?\""},{"sc":"mansion","w":"virginia","e":"smile","t":"Grandmother, she is a child of God now, just like us. She needs a family. I'm going to be her friend."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"Slowly, Loreen begins a new life. She's clean, fed, safe, and loved. The woman everyone gave up on is changing."}],"quote":{"text":"If any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.","who":"2 Corinthians 5:17","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Nobody is a hopeless case","text":"Everyone in the Rectangle had given up on Loreen. God hadn't. And Virginia didn't just pray for her; she opened her own home, even when her family and friends were shocked. Leaders believe people can change, and they make room for them to start again."},"think":"Is there someone everyone has 'given up on'? What would it look like to give them a second chance?","quiz":[{"q":"How did people in the Rectangle think of Loreen?","o":["As a hopeless case","As a leader","As a famous singer","As a rich woman"],"why":"Everyone had given up on her."},{"q":"What happened to Loreen when Rachel sang?","o":["She began to cry, and later prayed for a new life","She laughed","She left","She fell asleep"],"why":"God reached her through the song."},{"q":"What problem did Loreen have after the meeting?","o":["She had nowhere safe to go","She lost her shoes","She was hungry for cake","She couldn't find the tent"],"why":"Going back to the saloons would pull her back."},{"q":"What did Virginia do?","o":["Took Loreen to live in her own home","Gave her money and left","Told her to go to church","Called the police"],"why":"She asked what Jesus would do, and did it."},{"q":"How did Virginia's grandmother react?","o":["She was horrified","She was delighted","She didn't notice","She moved out"],"why":"Doing right can shock the people around you."}]},"ihs3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"mansion","n":"Virginia has a brother named {Rollin Page}. He's rich, handsome and popular. He spends his days at fancy clubs, playing cards and having fun. He has never worked a day in his life."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"Rollin admires Rachel. One day, he asks her to marry him."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rachel","e":"worried","t":"I'm sorry, Rollin. I can't say yes. You live only for yourself and your fun. Your life has no real purpose."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rollin","e":"shock","t":"No purpose? I've never thought about it like that..."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"Rachel's words stick in Rollin's mind. He can't stop thinking about them. One night, almost without meaning to, he walks into Mr Gray's tent in the Rectangle."},{"sc":"tent","n":"He sits at the back. He watches Rachel sing. He listens to the message. And something in his heart breaks open."},{"sc":"tent","w":"rollin","e":"worried","t":"I've wasted my whole life. Can God use someone like me?"},{"sc":"tent","n":"That night, Rollin Page gives his life to Jesus, in the same tent where Loreen found hope."},{"sc":"town","w":"rollin","e":"smile","t":"I know the rich young men at the clubs. Nobody preaches to them. Maybe that's my purpose: to go to the people I already know."},{"sc":"town","n":"So Rollin starts going back to his old clubs, not to waste time, but to talk to his old friends about real life and real purpose. Find out what happens next in Chapter 4!"}],"quote":{"text":"We are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works.","who":"Ephesians 2:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Find your purpose","text":"Rollin had money, looks and friends, but no purpose. Rachel's honest words made him think. When he found Jesus, he found his purpose right where he already was: reaching the people nobody else could reach. Leaders discover that God made them for good works, and often starts with the people already around them."},"think":"Who are 'your people', the friends, classmates or group you can reach better than anyone else?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Rollin Page spend his time at first?","o":["Having fun at fancy clubs, with no work and no purpose","Working on the railway","Preaching","Writing newspapers"],"why":"He lived only for himself."},{"q":"Why did Rachel say no to marrying Rollin?","o":["His life had no real purpose","He was poor","He was rude","She was too young"],"why":"Her honest answer made him think."},{"q":"Where did Rollin give his life to Jesus?","o":["In Mr Gray's tent in the Rectangle","In First Church","At his club","At home"],"why":"The same tent where Loreen found hope."},{"q":"Who did Rollin decide to reach?","o":["The rich young men at his old clubs","Only the poor","Nobody","Children"],"why":"People he could reach better than anyone."},{"q":"What does Ephesians 2:10 say we are created for?","o":["Good works","Fun","Money","Fame"],"why":"God made us with a purpose."}]}}},"ihs4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Virginia inherit?","o":["About a million dollars","A railway","A newspaper","A church"],"why":"A huge fortune for the 1890s."},{"q":"Which business did Virginia support?","o":["Edward Norman's honest newspaper","A saloon","An opera company","A bank"],"why":"She wanted the truth told in Raymond."},{"q":"\"Unto whomsoever much is given, of him shall be much ___.\"","o":["required","taken","forgotten","spent"],"why":"Luke 12:48."},{"q":"Why did Donald Marsh avoid politics at first?","o":["He thought it was dirty and preferred his quiet study","He was too young","He wasn't allowed","He was a saloon owner"],"why":"Then he asked what Jesus would do."},{"q":"What did the town vote on?","o":["Whether saloons could keep selling alcohol","A new mayor","A new church","School holidays"],"why":"The licence vote."},{"q":"Who won the vote?","o":["The saloons","The pledge-takers","Nobody","The railway"],"why":"Doing right doesn't always win at first."},{"q":"Who did Loreen protect?","o":["Virginia","Rachel","Maxwell","Rollin"],"why":"She stepped in front of the bottle."},{"q":"\"Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with ___.\"","o":["good","anger","money","silence"],"why":"Romans 12:21."},{"q":"What did Jasper Chase do with his pledge?","o":["Quietly stopped keeping it when success came","Kept it perfectly","Doubled it","Gave it to Rachel"],"why":"He drifted away."},{"q":"\"Ye did run well; who did ___ you?\"","o":["hinder","help","follow","find"],"why":"Galatians 5:7. Finish well!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Which pledge-taker turned back when it got costly?","o":["Jasper Chase","Rachel Winslow","Edward Norman","Virginia Page"],"why":"A warning to keep going when it costs."},"choices":[{"title":"Much given","q":"You win ₦50,000 in an inter-school essay competition. Everyone has ideas about how you should spend it.","o":[{"t":"Pray about it, give some to God and to someone in need, save some, and enjoy a little.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Virginia: it's money God trusted you with."},{"t":"Spend it all on yourself this week.","f":"Much given, much required. Ask what Jesus would do with it."},{"t":"Hide it and tell nobody.","f":"Hoarding isn't the same as stewarding. Use it well!"}]},{"title":"Step into the arena","q":"Your school is electing a new Senior Prefect. You'd be good at it, but you say, \"School politics is dirty. I'll stay out of it.\"","o":[{"t":"Run, or support a good candidate, and campaign honestly.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Donald Marsh: if good people stay out, someone else decides for everyone."},{"t":"Stay out and complain later.","f":"That's exactly what Marsh realised educated people kept doing."},{"t":"Run, but buy votes with snacks.","f":"You can't change the system by copying its worst habits."}]},{"title":"When you lose","q":"Your class campaigned to stop a harmful 'bullying initiation' for new students, but the seniors voted to keep it. Your friends want to give up.","o":[{"t":"Keep looking out for the new students, and keep working with teachers to end it.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Overcome evil with good, even after losing a vote."},{"t":"Give up. You tried.","f":"The pledge-takers lost the vote, but they didn't quit."},{"t":"Get revenge on the seniors.","f":"Revenge is being overcome by evil. Overcome it with good instead."}]},{"title":"Don't drift","q":"You and two friends promised to read the Bible together every morning. Since you got popular on social media, you've skipped it for weeks.","o":[{"t":"Admit you've drifted, message your friends, and start again tomorrow.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Jasper drifted quietly. You can turn back quietly too, and finish well."},{"t":"It's fine. You'll restart one day.","f":"\"Just for now\" is how Jasper drifted away."},{"t":"Quit the group so they won't ask.","f":"Hiding from accountability makes drifting easier."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"election","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use In His Steps, Chapter 4 in real life."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"💰 Much given, much required. Use money, big or small, the way Jesus would."},{"sc":"college","n":"🏛️ Step into the arena. Don't leave leadership to people who don't care."},{"sc":"election","n":"🗳️ Keep doing good when you lose. Overcome evil with good."},{"sc":"study","n":"📕 Don't drift. Finish what you start, even when it costs."}],"stops":{"ihs4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"mansion","n":"Virginia Page is very, very rich. Her parents left her an {inheritance} of about a million dollars, an enormous fortune in the 1890s."},{"sc":"mansion","w":"virginia","e":"worried","t":"I took the pledge. So what would Jesus do with a million dollars? Buy more dresses? Build a bigger house? I don't think so."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"First, she visits Edward Norman. His honest newspaper is losing money every week."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"virginia","e":"smile","t":"Mr Norman, Raymond needs a newspaper that tells the truth. I want to give you money to keep the Daily News going, the way Jesus would run it."},{"sc":"newsroom","w":"norman","e":"shock","t":"Miss Page... I don't know what to say. Thank you! Now we can keep going!"},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"Then Virginia goes to the Rectangle. She buys land there, right in the middle of the worst part of town."},{"sc":"rectangle","w":"virginia","e":"big","t":"We'll build something good here: a place where families can find help, learn, and be safe."},{"sc":"mansion","w":"grandmother","e":"frown","t":"Virginia! You're throwing your fortune away on newspapers and slums! What would your parents say?"},{"sc":"mansion","w":"virginia","e":"smile","t":"Grandmother, this money was given to me. I'm only borrowing it from God. I want to spend it the way He would."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"Her brother Rollin, the new Rollin, helps her plan. For the first time in their lives, their wealth has a purpose."}],"quote":{"text":"For unto whomsoever much is given, of him shall be much required.","who":"Luke 12:48","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Much given, much required","text":"Virginia didn't feel guilty for being rich, and she didn't waste it. She asked what Jesus would do with it, then used it to keep the truth alive and to bring hope to the poorest part of town. Leaders treat money as something God has trusted them with, not just something to enjoy."},"think":"Even a little money, like pocket money or a gift, is something God has given you. What would Jesus do with it?","quiz":[{"q":"How rich was Virginia Page?","o":["She inherited about a million dollars","She had a little pocket money","She was poor","She owned a railway"],"why":"An enormous fortune for the 1890s."},{"q":"Whose business did Virginia help first?","o":["Edward Norman's honest newspaper","The saloons","The opera company","The railway company"],"why":"She wanted Raymond to keep a paper that told the truth."},{"q":"What did she buy in the Rectangle?","o":["Land, to build a place of help and hope","A saloon","A theatre","Nothing"],"why":"Right in the middle of the worst part of town."},{"q":"How did her grandmother react?","o":["She thought Virginia was throwing her fortune away","She was proud","She gave more money","She didn't notice"],"why":"Not everyone understands generous choices."},{"q":"How did Virginia see her money?","o":["As something God had trusted her with","As hers to spend on herself","As a problem","As useless"],"why":"Much given, much required."}]},"ihs4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"{Donald Marsh} is the president of Lincoln College. He loves his books, his students and his quiet study. He has always stayed far away from town politics."},{"sc":"college","w":"marsh","e":"worried","t":"Politics is dirty. Arguments, shouting, newspapers attacking you. I'd much rather stay here and teach."},{"sc":"college","n":"But an election is coming. The town will vote on whether the saloons can keep selling alcohol. The saloons are destroying families in the Rectangle."},{"sc":"college","w":"marsh","e":"worried","t":"Educated men like me always say, 'Someone should do something about this town.' But we never do anything ourselves."},{"sc":"college","w":"marsh","e":"stern","t":"What would Jesus do? I don't believe He would hide in a comfortable study while the town suffered. I have to get involved."},{"sc":"town","n":"So the quiet professor steps out. He speaks at public meetings. He works with Maxwell, Norman and the others to campaign for a cleaner, safer Raymond."},{"sc":"town","n":"It's hard and uncomfortable. Some people mock him. Some old friends stop speaking to him. But he keeps going."},{"sc":"town","n":"Meanwhile, Milton Wright, a businessman who took the pledge, changes the way he runs his shops. He treats his workers like partners and pays them fairly."},{"sc":"town","w":"marsh","e":"smile","t":"I always taught my students to be good citizens. Now I'm finally being one myself."}],"quote":{"text":"When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice.","who":"Proverbs 29:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't leave leadership to the wrong people","text":"Marsh thought politics was too dirty for good people. Then he realised: if good people stay out, the town is left to those who don't care about it. Leaders step into uncomfortable places, like elections, committees and public debates, when that's where good is needed."},"think":"Is there a class election, student council or community group you've avoided because it seems 'too messy'? What would Jesus do?","quiz":[{"q":"Who was Donald Marsh?","o":["The president of Lincoln College","A saloon owner","A newspaper boy","A railway worker"],"why":"A quiet professor who loved his books."},{"q":"What did Marsh think about politics at first?","o":["That it was dirty, and he wanted to stay away from it","That it was fun","That it was easy","That only kings should do it"],"why":"He preferred his quiet study."},{"q":"What was the town election about?","o":["Whether saloons could keep selling alcohol","Choosing a new pastor","Building a railway","A singing competition"],"why":"The saloons were destroying families."},{"q":"What did Marsh decide to do?","o":["Get involved and campaign for a better town","Leave Raymond","Stay in his study","Open a saloon"],"why":"He didn't think Jesus would hide while the town suffered."},{"q":"How did Milton Wright change his business?","o":["He treated his workers like partners and paid them fairly","He closed it","He raised his prices","He fired everyone"],"why":"The pledge reached the shop floor too."}]},"ihs4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"election","n":"The day of the {licence vote} arrives. All over Raymond, people go to vote. The pledge-takers have worked hard for weeks."},{"sc":"election","n":"But that evening, the results come in. The saloons have won. They can keep selling alcohol in the Rectangle."},{"sc":"election","w":"norman","e":"worried","t":"We lost. After everything."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"That night, the Rectangle is wild. The saloons celebrate their victory. Crowds of drunk men spill into the streets, shouting and throwing things."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"Virginia and Rachel are in the Rectangle, helping at the tent, with Loreen beside them. As they walk past a saloon, an angry crowd gathers."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"Someone throws a heavy bottle from an upstairs window, straight towards Virginia. Loreen sees it coming. She steps in front of her friend."},{"sc":"rectangle","n":"The bottle hits Loreen. She falls. Virginia is unharmed. But Loreen is badly hurt."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"They carry her to Virginia's house. Virginia and Rachel stay beside her. Loreen dies peacefully that night, safe, loved, and at home."},{"sc":"church","n":"The whole town is shaken. At Loreen's funeral, rich and poor come together to honour the woman who once was called a hopeless case, and who gave her life for her friend."},{"sc":"church","w":"virginia","e":"worried","t":"Loreen gave her life for me. Now I'll give the rest of mine for the Rectangle."}],"quote":{"text":"Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.","who":"Romans 12:21","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't let losing make you quit","text":"The pledge-takers did everything right, and still lost the vote. Then they lost Loreen. They could have given up. Instead, the sadness made them more determined. Loreen, once 'hopeless', showed the greatest love of all. Leaders keep doing good even when they lose, and they turn grief into deeper commitment."},"think":"Have you ever worked hard for something good and still lost? What helped you keep going, or what could?","quiz":[{"q":"What happened in the licence vote?","o":["The saloons won","The saloons were closed","Nobody voted","It was cancelled"],"why":"The pledge-takers lost, despite their hard work."},{"q":"What happened in the Rectangle that night?","o":["Drunk crowds celebrated wildly in the streets","Everyone went to church","It was very quiet","There was a concert"],"why":"The saloons celebrated."},{"q":"What did Loreen do when the bottle was thrown?","o":["Stepped in front of Virginia to protect her","Ran away","Threw it back","Called the police"],"why":"She gave her life for her friend."},{"q":"How did Loreen die?","o":["Peacefully that night, safe and loved at Virginia's home","Alone on the street","In prison","She didn't die"],"why":"She was surrounded by friends who loved her."},{"q":"What did Virginia decide after losing Loreen?","o":["To give the rest of her life for the Rectangle","To leave Raymond","To stop helping","To blame Rachel"],"why":"Grief turned into deeper commitment."}]},"ihs4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"study","n":"Not everyone who took the pledge kept it. {Jasper Chase} was a popular writer in Raymond. He stood up with the others on that first Sunday."},{"sc":"study","n":"Jasper admired Rachel and hoped to marry her, but she didn't feel the same way about him, and she told him so kindly."},{"sc":"study","n":"Then a big {publisher} offers Jasper a deal for his new novel. It means money, fame, and praise from important people."},{"sc":"study","w":"jasper","e":"worried","t":"If I keep asking 'What would Jesus do?', I might have to change my book, or turn down this deal. That's asking too much."},{"sc":"study","w":"jasper","e":"frown","t":"I'll just... stop asking the question. Just for now."},{"sc":"study","n":"And so Jasper Chase quietly turns away from his pledge. Nobody makes a big announcement. He just stops."},{"sc":"study","n":"His book sells well. People praise him. But Maxwell is sad when he hears, and Jasper himself doesn't seem any happier."},{"sc":"study","w":"maxwell","e":"worried","t":"He started so well. The pledge was too costly for him in the end."},{"sc":"study","n":"Rachel, Virginia, Norman, Powers and Marsh all paid a price for keeping the pledge. Jasper chose the easier road. The story leaves us to ask: which road will WE choose?"}],"quote":{"text":"Ye did run well; who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth?","who":"Galatians 5:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Finish what you start","text":"Jasper started just like the others. But when keeping the pledge got costly, he quietly stopped asking the question. Most people don't fall away in one big moment. They drift, one small 'just for now' at a time. Leaders keep their commitments when it costs them, and they notice when they start to drift."},"think":"Is there a promise you made to God or to yourself that you've slowly drifted from? What 'just for now' do you need to stop?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Jasper Chase's job?","o":["A popular writer","A singer","An editor","A railway boss"],"why":"He wrote novels."},{"q":"What tempted Jasper to stop keeping the pledge?","o":["A big publishing deal with money and fame","A lion","A storm","His friends' advice"],"why":"Success came calling."},{"q":"How did Jasper turn away from his pledge?","o":["He quietly stopped asking the question","He made a big speech","He left town","He burned his books"],"why":"Drifting is usually quiet."},{"q":"How did Maxwell feel when he heard?","o":["Sad","Happy","Angry","He didn't care"],"why":"\"He started so well.\""},{"q":"What does Galatians 5:7 ask?","o":["\"Ye did run well; who did hinder you?\"","\"Who is the fastest?\"","\"Where are you going?\"","\"Why are you tired?\""],"why":"Starting well matters, but so does finishing."}]}}},"ihs5":{"challenge":[{"q":"Which city did the pledge travel to?","o":["Chicago","Lagos","London","Raymond"],"why":"A city of millions."},{"q":"Who carried the question to Chicago?","o":["Rev. Calvin Bruce","Edward Norman","Jasper Chase","Mr Clark"],"why":"He saw it in Raymond and took it home."},{"q":"What did Bruce give up?","o":["His rich, comfortable church","His Bible","His family","His train ticket"],"why":"To live among the poor."},{"q":"Who joined Bruce at the Settlement?","o":["Bishop Hampton","Virginia Page","Alexander Powers","Rollin Page"],"why":"A bishop chose to step down too."},{"q":"\"He made himself of no ___, and took upon him the form of a servant.\"","o":["reputation","money","power","friends"],"why":"Philippians 2:7."},{"q":"What skill did Felicia use?","o":["Cooking","Singing","Writing","Building"],"why":"She started with what was in her hand."},{"q":"Why did Felicia's life change?","o":["Her family lost everything","She won a prize","She moved to Raymond","She got married"],"why":"Loss became a new beginning."},{"q":"\"All things work together for ___ to them that love God.\"","o":["good","money","fun","fame"],"why":"Romans 8:28."},{"q":"How did Maxwell answer the angry worker?","o":["He listened, admitted what was true, and shared real stories","He argued loudly","He left","He ignored him"],"why":"A soft answer turns away wrath."},{"q":"\"A soft answer turneth away ___.\"","o":["wrath","friends","money","time"],"why":"Proverbs 15:1."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Felicia said: \"When I was rich, I felt ___.\"","o":["useless","happy","tired","brave"],"why":"Now she had nothing, and felt more useful than ever!"},"choices":[{"title":"Pass it on","q":"Your school's 'Kindness Week' project changed the whole atmosphere. A teacher from another school asks how you did it.","o":[{"t":"Share everything, and offer to help them start their own.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Calvin Bruce, carry the good idea to new places."},{"t":"Keep it secret so your school stays special.","f":"Good things are meant to spread."},{"t":"Charge them for the idea.","f":"Freely you received, freely give."}]},{"title":"Stepping down","q":"The 'cool' group invites you to sit with them every break. But you've been helping lead the junior Bible club during that break.","o":[{"t":"Keep serving the juniors, and stay friendly with the cool group at other times.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like the Bishop, sometimes leaders step down to lift others up."},{"t":"Drop the juniors. Popularity matters more.","f":"That's climbing up instead of serving down."},{"t":"Bring the cool group to mock the juniors.","f":"Never use others to raise your own status."}]},{"title":"What's in your hand","q":"Your family's business collapsed this year and money is very tight. You feel embarrassed and want to hide from everyone.","o":[{"t":"Use a skill you have, like baking, tutoring or braiding, to help at home and serve others.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Felicia: start with what's in your hand. There's no shame in honest work."},{"t":"Pretend everything is fine and borrow money to look rich.","f":"That builds a fake life on debt."},{"t":"Give up on your dreams.","f":"All things can work together for good. This isn't the end."}]},{"title":"The angry critic","q":"A man on your street says loudly, \"Churches only want your money! Pastors are all thieves!\" Your friends want to argue with him.","o":[{"t":"Listen calmly, admit some churches do fail, and share what real faith has done for you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! A soft answer turns away wrath, just as Maxwell found."},{"t":"Shout back and insult him.","f":"Grievous words stir up anger."},{"t":"Agree with him to avoid trouble.","f":"Be honest about failures, but don't deny the truth."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"chicago","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use In His Steps, Chapter 5 in real life."},{"sc":"chicago","n":"🚂 Pass it on. Good examples travel further than you think."},{"sc":"settlement","n":"🪣 Step down to lift up. Leaders serve, even when it costs them status."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"🍲 Start with what's in your hand. A simple skill can become a calling."},{"sc":"hall","n":"🕊️ Answer anger with honesty and love. Listen first. Admit what's true."}],"stops":{"ihs5s1":{"story":[{"sc":"town","n":"News of the pledge in Raymond starts to spread. A pastor from the great city of {Chicago} comes to see it for himself. His name is {Calvin Bruce}, an old friend of Henry Maxwell."},{"sc":"study","w":"bruce","e":"shock","t":"Henry, is it true? Your editor dropped the Sunday paper? Your railway boss gave up his job? Your best singer sings in a slum tent?"},{"sc":"study","w":"maxwell","e":"smile","t":"All true, Calvin. And much more. Come and see."},{"sc":"newsroom","n":"Bruce visits Norman's newspaper, meets Alexander Powers, hears Rachel sing in the Rectangle, and sees Virginia's plans for the poor."},{"sc":"rectangle","w":"bruce","e":"worried","t":"I preach to rich, comfortable people every Sunday. I've never asked my church to do anything like this. I've never done anything like this myself."},{"sc":"chicago","n":"Bruce takes the train back to Chicago. But he can't stop thinking about it. He goes to see his friend {Bishop} Hampton, a respected church leader."},{"sc":"chicago","w":"bruce","e":"worried","t":"Bishop, I've seen something in Raymond I can't forget. People are really asking 'What would Jesus do?', and then doing it."},{"sc":"chicago","w":"bishop","e":"worried","t":"Then perhaps the question has come to Chicago for us too, Calvin. The poor of this city are suffering right under our windows."}],"quote":{"text":"Ye shall be witnesses unto me both in Jerusalem, and in all Judaea... and unto the uttermost part of the earth.","who":"Acts 1:8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Real change spreads","text":"The pledge started with fifty people in one church. It didn't stay there. When Calvin Bruce saw changed lives, he carried the question home to a city of millions. Leaders don't just change their own little world. Their example travels further than they ever imagined."},"think":"Who might be watching what you do, and carry it somewhere you'll never go?","quiz":[{"q":"Who came from Chicago to visit Raymond?","o":["Rev. Calvin Bruce, Maxwell's old friend","Jasper Chase","Mr Gray","Loreen"],"why":"He came to see the pledge for himself."},{"q":"What surprised Bruce most?","o":["People were really living out 'What would Jesus do?'","The size of the church","The weather","The trains"],"why":"Real lives had changed."},{"q":"What did Bruce realise about himself?","o":["He had never asked his church, or himself, to live like this","He was a great singer","He wanted to move to Raymond","He was rich"],"why":"Honest reflection is the start of change."},{"q":"Who did Bruce go to see in Chicago?","o":["Bishop Hampton","The Mayor","Edward Norman","Felicia"],"why":"A respected church leader and friend."},{"q":"What does this stop teach?","o":["Real change spreads further than you expect","Stay in your own town","Trains are fast","Don't visit friends"],"why":"Fifty people in Raymond started something big."}]},"ihs5s2":{"story":[{"sc":"chicago","n":"Calvin Bruce is the pastor of one of the richest churches in Chicago. Beautiful building. Wealthy members. A comfortable salary and a fine house."},{"sc":"chicago","n":"Not far away are streets where families live crammed into dark rooms, children go hungry, and nobody from the rich churches ever visits."},{"sc":"chicago","w":"bruce","e":"stern","t":"What would Jesus do, if He were pastor of my church? I don't think He would stay in the comfortable part of town while the poor suffered a few streets away."},{"sc":"chicago","n":"So Bruce does something nobody expects. He resigns from his big, wealthy church."},{"sc":"chicago","w":"bishop","e":"smile","t":"Calvin, I'm coming with you. I've been a bishop in a fine house for years. It's time I lived among the people I'm supposed to serve."},{"sc":"settlement","n":"Together, the pastor and the bishop move into a {Settlement}, a house right in the middle of one of the poorest neighbourhoods in Chicago."},{"sc":"settlement","n":"They live there with the people. They open the doors for classes, meetings, meals and help. They visit the sick. They learn the names of the children."},{"sc":"settlement","n":"Many of their rich friends are shocked. \"A bishop living in the slums? What a waste!\" But the people of the neighbourhood begin to trust them."},{"sc":"settlement","w":"bishop","e":"smile","t":"I've preached about Jesus for thirty years. I think I'm only now beginning to understand Him."}],"quote":{"text":"But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant.","who":"Philippians 2:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Leaders go down, not just up","text":"Most people climb towards comfort, status and the 'better' part of town. Bruce and the Bishop went the other way, because that's what Jesus did. He left heaven to live among us. Leaders who follow in His steps are willing to step down, so they can lift others up."},"think":"Is there a way you could 'step down', giving up some comfort or status, to serve someone who needs you?","quiz":[{"q":"What kind of church did Calvin Bruce lead?","o":["One of the richest churches in Chicago","A tiny village church","A tent church","No church"],"why":"Comfort, wealth and a fine house."},{"q":"What did Bruce do after asking the question?","o":["Resigned from his big church","Built a bigger church","Moved to Raymond","Became an editor"],"why":"He didn't think Jesus would stay comfortable while others suffered."},{"q":"Who went with him?","o":["Bishop Hampton","Jasper Chase","Mr Clark","Mrs Winslow"],"why":"A senior church leader chose to serve too."},{"q":"Where did they go to live?","o":["In a Settlement house in a poor neighbourhood","In a palace","On a farm","In a hotel"],"why":"They lived among the people they served."},{"q":"How did their rich friends react?","o":["They were shocked","They all followed","They didn't notice","They gave them awards"],"why":"Stepping down looks foolish to some people."}]},"ihs5s3":{"story":[{"sc":"mansion","n":"{Felicia Sterling} grows up in one of the richest homes in Chicago. Servants, fine clothes, parties. But Felicia has one unusual love: cooking."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"Then, in a single day, everything changes. Her father loses his entire fortune. Not long afterwards, he dies, and the family is left with nothing."},{"sc":"mansion","w":"felicia","e":"worried","t":"Everything's gone: the house, the money, our friends. What do I have left?"},{"sc":"settlement","n":"Felicia goes to the Settlement, where Bruce and the Bishop are working. She asks herself the question."},{"sc":"settlement","w":"felicia","e":"smile","t":"What would Jesus do with what I have? I can't give money any more. But I can cook! And many families here don't know how to make good, cheap, healthy meals."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"So the rich girl who lost everything puts on an apron. She opens a kitchen at the Settlement and teaches poor women and girls how to cook nourishing food on very little money."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"She also cooks for people who are sick or too old to cook for themselves. Her kitchen becomes one of the happiest places in the neighbourhood."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"felicia","e":"big","t":"When I was rich, I felt useless. Now I have nothing, and I've never felt more useful in my life!"}],"quote":{"text":"And we know that all things work together for good to them that love God.","who":"Romans 8:28","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Start with what's in your hand","text":"Felicia lost money, status and friends. She could have sunk into despair. Instead she asked, \"What do I still have?\" A simple skill, cooking, became her way to serve and lead. Leaders don't wait for perfect circumstances. They start with what's in their hand."},"think":"What simple skill do you have, like braiding hair, cooking, fixing things or explaining maths, that could help someone?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Felicia's unusual love as a rich girl?","o":["Cooking","Horse riding","Singing opera","Writing books"],"why":"A simple skill that would become her calling."},{"q":"What happened to the Sterling family?","o":["Her father lost his fortune, and the family was left with nothing","They became richer","They moved to Raymond","They opened a saloon"],"why":"Everything changed in one day."},{"q":"What question did Felicia ask?","o":["\"What would Jesus do with what I have?\"","\"Why me?\"","\"Who is to blame?\"","\"How do I get rich again?\""],"why":"She started with what was in her hand."},{"q":"What did Felicia do at the Settlement?","o":["Opened a kitchen and taught people to cook healthy food cheaply","Sang in the choir","Ran the newspaper","Sold dresses"],"why":"Her skill became her service."},{"q":"How did Felicia feel at the end?","o":["More useful than ever before","Miserable","Angry","Bored"],"why":"All things work together for good."}]},"ihs5s4":{"story":[{"sc":"hall","n":"Henry Maxwell comes to Chicago to visit Bruce and the Bishop. They ask him to speak at a meeting in the Settlement hall."},{"sc":"hall","n":"The hall is packed with working men. Many have lost their jobs. Some are angry with rich people, angry with the government, and very angry with churches."},{"sc":"hall","w":"hallworker","e":"frown","t":"Churches! Big buildings full of rich people singing nice songs, while our children go hungry! What has the church ever done for us?"},{"sc":"hall","n":"Some people in the hall shout in agreement. Maxwell could get defensive. He could argue back. Instead, he listens quietly until the man finishes."},{"sc":"hall","w":"maxwell","e":"worried","t":"My friend, you are partly right. Too often the church has sung songs and not lived them. A man once stood up in MY church and told me exactly that."},{"sc":"hall","w":"maxwell","e":"smile","t":"He changed my life. Now some of us are trying to ask, before everything we do: 'What would Jesus do?' And then do it."},{"sc":"hall","n":"He tells them about the stranger, about Norman and Powers, about Loreen and the Rectangle. The room grows quiet."},{"sc":"hall","n":"Then Rachel, who has come with him, stands and sings. The same voice that silenced the Rectangle silences the angry hall."},{"sc":"hall","w":"hallworker","e":"smile","t":"If that's what Christians are really like... maybe I've been wrong about some of them."}],"quote":{"text":"A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.","who":"Proverbs 15:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Answer anger with honesty and love","text":"The angry worker said some hard things, and some of them were true. Maxwell didn't argue or defend himself. He admitted the church's failures, told the truth about his own, and pointed to real changed lives. Leaders listen to critics, admit what's true, and answer with love and action."},"think":"When someone criticises your church, school or family, how could you listen first before defending?","quiz":[{"q":"Who was in the Settlement hall?","o":["Working men, many of them angry and out of work","Rich bankers","Children","Nobody"],"why":"People who felt forgotten by the church."},{"q":"What did the angry worker say about churches?","o":["They were full of rich people singing while children went hungry","They were too small","They were too far","They had bad music"],"why":"Some of it was true."},{"q":"How did Maxwell first respond?","o":["He listened quietly","He shouted back","He walked out","He called the police"],"why":"Listening comes before answering."},{"q":"What did Maxwell admit?","o":["That the church had often sung songs without living them","That he was perfect","That the workers were lazy","Nothing"],"why":"Honesty disarms anger."},{"q":"Who sang at the meeting?","o":["Rachel Winslow","Felicia","The Bishop","Mr Gray"],"why":"Her voice silenced another angry room."}]}}},"ihs6":{"challenge":[{"q":"What question started everything in Raymond?","o":["\"What would Jesus do?\"","\"Who is the richest?\"","\"Where is the train?\"","\"How much does it pay?\""],"why":"Four words that changed a town."},{"q":"Who first asked First Church about living out their songs?","o":["A homeless stranger","Edward Norman","The Bishop","Rachel"],"why":"Remember Chapter 1?"},{"q":"What did Norman say about his newspaper after one year?","o":["It became trusted all over the state","It closed","It made him rich","He sold it"],"why":"Integrity built trust."},{"q":"\"They that sow in tears shall reap in ___.\"","o":["joy","money","fame","sorrow"],"why":"Psalm 126:5."},{"q":"Why did Rachel finally say yes to Rollin?","o":["They now shared the same purpose: following Jesus","He was rich","He was famous","Her mother told her to"],"why":"Walking the same road."},{"q":"\"Be ye not unequally ___ together with unbelievers.\"","o":["yoked","seated","dressed","named"],"why":"2 Corinthians 6:14."},{"q":"What did Jesus say His followers are like?","o":["A city on a hill that can't be hidden","A secret","A sleeping lion","A closed door"],"why":"Matthew 5:14."},{"q":"Where did Maxwell ask what would happen if every Christian took the pledge?","o":["A huge gathering in Chicago","The Rectangle tent","His study only","Norman's office"],"why":"The question kept growing."},{"q":"How does In His Steps end?","o":["With the question for every reader","With a battle","With Raymond destroyed","With a party"],"why":"It's your turn now."},{"q":"\"He that saith he abideth in him ought himself also so to ___, even as he walked.\"","o":["walk","run","sing","write"],"why":"1 John 2:6."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What do the letters WWJD stand for?","o":["What Would Jesus Do?","We Walk Just Daily","Wise Words Just Do","Win With Joy Daily"],"why":"Ask it, then do it!"},"choices":[{"title":"Look back","q":"It's the end of the school year. You made some good choices and some bad ones.","o":[{"t":"Honestly write down what doing right cost you, and what it gave you, and set goals for next year.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Count the cost and count the gain, like the people of Raymond."},{"t":"Only remember the bad things and feel terrible.","f":"Look at the whole picture, including what God gave you."},{"t":"Don't think about it at all.","f":"Leaders reflect, so they can grow."}]},{"title":"Walking the same road","q":"Someone in SS2 keeps asking you to be their boyfriend or girlfriend. They're popular, but they say faith is \"not a big deal\".","o":[{"t":"Politely say no, and focus on good friendships for now.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Rachel, wait for people who walk the same road. For now, build strong friendships."},{"t":"Say yes because they're popular.","f":"Rachel didn't choose Rollin for looks or status."},{"t":"Say yes and hope to change them.","f":"Rachel waited until Rollin's LIFE had changed, not just his words."}]},{"title":"A city on a hill","q":"Your class has become known as the class that doesn't cheat in exams. Other classes mock you and call you \"church class\".","o":[{"t":"Keep being honest, and be kind to those who mock.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! A city on a hill can't be hidden. Your light is working."},{"t":"Start cheating so people stop mocking.","f":"Don't hide the light. Let it shine."},{"t":"Mock the other classes back.","f":"Light shines best with kindness."}]},{"title":"My own pledge","q":"You've finished In His Steps. Your youth leader asks: \"Will you take the pledge yourself?\"","o":[{"t":"Yes. Write it down, pick a time period, and ask a friend to keep you accountable.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Now it's your turn to walk in His steps."},{"t":"Maybe later. It sounds hard.","f":"Jasper Chase said \"just for now\". Don't let 'later' become 'never'."},{"t":"Say yes, but don't really mean it.","f":"The pledge has two parts: ask, AND do."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"dream","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use In His Steps, Chapter 6 in real life."},{"sc":"church","n":"📅 Count the cost, and count the gain. Doing right costs something, and gives you more."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"💍 Choose people who walk your road, in friendships now and one day in marriage."},{"sc":"hall","n":"🏮 Shine like a city on a hill. Your example can't be hidden."},{"sc":"dream","n":"👣 Take the pledge. Ask \"What would Jesus do?\", then do it, every day."}],"stops":{"ihs6s1":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"It's the {anniversary} of the pledge. One year ago, a dying stranger asked First Church a question. Today, the church is full again."},{"sc":"church","w":"maxwell","e":"smile","t":"A year ago, about fifty of us promised to ask 'What would Jesus do?' before everything. Let's hear what happened."},{"sc":"church","w":"norman","e":"smile","t":"My newspaper lost money for months. But today it's trusted all over the state. I'd never go back."},{"sc":"church","w":"powers","e":"smile","t":"I lost my big job and some of my friends. But I sleep with a clear conscience. That's worth more than any salary."},{"sc":"church","w":"virginia","e":"smile","t":"My money used to just sit in a bank. Now it's building homes and a hall in the Rectangle. Loreen's memory lives on there."},{"sc":"church","w":"rachel","e":"smile","t":"I turned down fame. But my voice has never been used for anything more beautiful than what God has done with it this year."},{"sc":"church","n":"Not everyone kept the pledge. Some, like Jasper Chase, quietly turned back. But those who kept it say the same thing: it cost a lot, and it was worth everything."},{"sc":"church","w":"maxwell","e":"big","t":"We thought we were giving things up. We were actually finding out what it really means to live."}],"quote":{"text":"They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.","who":"Psalm 126:5","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Count the cost, and count the gain","text":"After a year, the pledge-takers could see the full picture. Each lost something: money, a job, fame, friends. Each gained something greater: trust, peace, purpose and joy. Leaders look honestly at both the cost and the reward, and they keep going."},"think":"Look back at your last year. What did doing the right thing cost you? What did it give you?","quiz":[{"q":"How long had the pledge lasted?","o":["One year","One week","One month","Ten years"],"why":"A full year of asking the question."},{"q":"What had happened to Norman's newspaper?","o":["It lost money at first, but became trusted all over the state","It closed","It became a saloon","Nothing"],"why":"Integrity built trust over time."},{"q":"What did Powers say was worth more than a salary?","o":["A clear conscience","A bigger house","A new train","A medal"],"why":"Peace with God."},{"q":"What was Virginia's money doing now?","o":["Building homes and a hall in the Rectangle","Sitting in a bank","Buying dresses","Funding the saloons"],"why":"Much given, much required."},{"q":"What did those who kept the pledge say?","o":["It cost a lot, and was worth everything","It was easy","They regretted it","Nothing changed"],"why":"Sow in tears, reap in joy."}]},"ihs6s2":{"story":[{"sc":"parlour","n":"Remember Rollin Page? A year ago, Rachel said no when he asked to marry her, because his life had no purpose."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"Since that night in the tent, Rollin has changed completely. He spends his time reaching the young men at the rich clubs, helping Virginia in the Rectangle, and asking the question every day."},{"sc":"parlour","n":"Rachel has watched him. Not his words, but his life."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rollin","e":"worried","t":"Rachel, I know you said no once. I was a different man then. Would you think about it again?"},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rachel","e":"big","t":"Rollin, I said no because you had no purpose. Now we share the same purpose: following Jesus. Yes!"},{"sc":"parlour","n":"Rachel and Rollin become engaged. They plan to keep serving together, her voice and his witness, in the Rectangle and beyond."},{"sc":"parlour","w":"rachel","e":"smile","t":"I didn't want a man who was just handsome and rich. I wanted someone walking the same road as me."}],"quote":{"text":"Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers.","who":"2 Corinthians 6:14","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Choose people who walk your road","text":"Rachel didn't decide based on looks or money. She waited until she saw that Rollin's life, not just his words, was following the same Jesus she followed. For teens, that starts with friendships: choose close friends, and one day a partner, who are walking the same road."},"think":"Who are your closest friends? Are they walking the same road as you? Are you helping each other follow Jesus?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Rachel first say no to Rollin?","o":["His life had no purpose","He was poor","He was rude","She wanted to be famous"],"why":"Remember Chapter 3?"},{"q":"How had Rollin changed?","o":["He was serving others and following Jesus every day","He was richer","He had moved away","He hadn't changed"],"why":"His life, not just his words, had changed."},{"q":"What did Rachel watch?","o":["His life, not just his words","His bank account","His clothes","His car"],"why":"Actions show the heart."},{"q":"What did Rachel say they now shared?","o":["The same purpose: following Jesus","The same house","The same job","The same friends"],"why":"Walking the same road."},{"q":"What is the main lesson for teens now?","o":["Choose close friends who walk the same road as you","Get married early","Only date rich people","Don't have friends"],"why":"It starts with friendships."}]},"ihs6s3":{"story":[{"sc":"chicago","n":"Maxwell is invited to speak to a huge gathering of Christians in Chicago. Pastors and church members come from far and wide."},{"sc":"hall","w":"maxwell","e":"stern","t":"What would happen if every church member in this country asked 'What would Jesus do?' and then did it?"},{"sc":"hall","w":"maxwell","e":"stern","t":"Would businesses still cheat their workers? Would newspapers still print what harms people? Would children still go hungry a few streets from our churches?"},{"sc":"hall","n":"The room is silent. Many people feel uncomfortable. Some are inspired. Some decide, right there, to take the pledge themselves."},{"sc":"settlement","n":"At the Settlement, Bruce, the Bishop and Felicia keep serving. More helpers arrive every month. Rich and poor work side by side."},{"sc":"town","n":"Back in Raymond, the Rectangle is slowly changing. There's a new hall, new homes, classes for children and mothers. A town once divided is learning to be one."},{"sc":"hall","w":"maxwell","e":"smile","t":"Jesus said His followers are like a city on a hill. You can't hide it. When people really live like Him, everyone can see the light."}],"quote":{"text":"Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.","who":"Matthew 5:14","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Imagine if everyone did","text":"Maxwell asked a huge question: what if EVERY Christian really lived this way? Businesses, newspapers, schools and governments would change. It starts with a few people, like the fifty in Raymond, whose light can't be hidden. Leaders dream big about what could change, and they start with themselves."},"think":"What would change in your school if every Christian student asked 'What would Jesus do?' for one month?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Maxwell speak to a huge gathering?","o":["Chicago","Raymond","London","The Rectangle"],"why":"The question kept travelling."},{"q":"What big question did Maxwell ask?","o":["What would happen if every church member asked the question and did it?","Who wants to be rich?","Where is the train?","Who is the best singer?"],"why":"A question for the whole church."},{"q":"How did the audience react?","o":["Some were uncomfortable, some inspired, and some took the pledge","Everyone left","They laughed","They slept"],"why":"Hard questions stir people."},{"q":"What was changing in the Rectangle?","o":["New homes, a hall, and classes for families","More saloons","Nothing","It was knocked down"],"why":"Slow, real change."},{"q":"What did Jesus compare His followers to?","o":["A city on a hill that can't be hidden","A hidden treasure","A small seed","A dark room"],"why":"Matthew 5:14."}]},"ihs6s4":{"story":[{"sc":"dream","n":"That night, Maxwell can't sleep. He kneels by his window and prays. And as he prays, he sees something like a {vision} of the future."},{"sc":"dream","n":"He sees Rachel singing for crowds of people who need hope. He sees Virginia's work in the Rectangle growing. He sees Norman's newspaper inspiring others across the land."},{"sc":"dream","n":"He sees Felicia and the Settlement full of children, laughing and learning. He sees the Bishop and Bruce surrounded by people whose lives have changed."},{"sc":"dream","n":"He sees churches everywhere waking up, with people asking the question in offices, schools, shops and homes."},{"sc":"dream","n":"But he also sees people who hear the question and turn away, because it costs too much."},{"sc":"dream","w":"maxwell","e":"worried","t":"Lord, will Your people really follow You? Will we walk in Your steps, whatever it costs?"},{"sc":"dream","n":"As the sun rises, Maxwell's heart is full of hope. The question has been asked. Now it's up to each person to answer it."},{"sc":"dream","n":"THE END of In His Steps. One question, asked by a homeless stranger, changed a church, a town and a city. Now the question comes to you."},{"sc":"dream","n":"Before you decide anything today, at school, at home or online, ask it: What would Jesus do? And then, do it."}],"quote":{"text":"He that saith he abideth in him ought himself also so to walk, even as he walked.","who":"1 John 2:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Now it's your turn","text":"The book doesn't end with everything fixed. It ends with a question for every reader. The people of Raymond have walked their year. Now it's your turn to ask, \"What would Jesus do?\", and then do it, whatever it costs. That is what it means to lead by following in His steps."},"think":"Write your own pledge: for one week (or one month, or one year), what will you ask before every decision? Who will help you keep it?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Maxwell see as he prayed?","o":["Something like a vision of the future","A lion","A storm","A train"],"why":"A picture of what could be."},{"q":"What did Maxwell see churches doing in his vision?","o":["Waking up and asking the question everywhere","Closing down","Fighting each other","Building bigger buildings"],"why":"His hope for the future."},{"q":"What did Maxwell also see some people doing?","o":["Hearing the question and turning away because it cost too much","Flying","Singing","Sleeping"],"why":"Not everyone will follow."},{"q":"How does the book end?","o":["With the question for every reader","With a wedding","With a war","With a storm"],"why":"Now it's your turn."},{"q":"\"He that saith he abideth in him ought himself also so to walk, even as he ___.\"","o":["walked","talked","sang","slept"],"why":"1 John 2:6. Walk as Jesus walked."}]}}}});
